@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# Design
+
+## Context
+
+The service in `src/rental.ts` keeps equipment in a `Map` and per-item reserved periods in another `Map`; `book` already tests overlap with `start < r.end && r.start < end`. Period validation lives in `parsePeriod`.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:**
+- Reuse the existing period validation and overlap rule so availability and `book` can never disagree.
+
+**Non-Goals:**
+- Cancellation, prices in the result, or returning equipment objects.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Extract the overlap test into a small helper used by both `book` and `availability`, rather than duplicating it.
+- Validate `kind` when provided, with the same rule as `addEquipment`, so a typo throws instead of silently returning an empty list.
+- Sort with the default string comparison (`.sort()`), giving a deterministic order independent of insertion.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- Linear scan over all equipment per query → acceptable for an in-memory desk-sized inventory.
